<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Telebras rebounds in NY.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Telebras rebounds in NY.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telebras SA shares recovered on Thursday and climbed higher in active New York Stock Exchange trade on receding market concern over a scandal allegedly involving a leading Brazilian Cabinet minister, traders said.</p>
<p>In midsession NYSE trade, Telebras American depositary receipts were up three to 124-3/4.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the ADRs had tumbled 4-3/8 after reports that Communications Minister Sergio Motta allegedly helped to buy votes for a bill that would allow President Fernando Henrique Cardoso to run for re-election.</p>
</text>
